This is a 55-year-old male.

467
00:28:56,780 --> 00:29:00,720
He has this lesion on his
back. His wife wants you to

468
00:29:00,720 --> 00:29:03,540
biopsy it. But he says
the lesion's been present

469
00:29:03,540 --> 00:29:06,600
since birth, right? He doesn't
believe it's changed in

470
00:29:06,600 --> 00:29:10,260
any way, shape, or form.
So do you biopsy it or not?

471
00:29:10,500 --> 00:29:13,660
Do you recommend the
biopsy? Yes or no?

472
00:29:14,320 --> 00:29:18,100
Look at this. It's very
well defined, right?

473
00:29:18,100 --> 00:29:21,160
The pigmentation is
very, very uniform.

474
00:29:22,240 --> 00:29:25,080
No, you don't biopsy it. What

475
00:29:25,080 --> 00:29:26,520
do you call this
type of lesion?

476
00:29:26,880 --> 00:29:31,240
It's a congenital nevus
or congenital mole. And

477
00:29:31,240 --> 00:29:33,860
it's present since birth.
It's highly pigmented.

478
00:29:33,860 --> 00:29:36,300
You can actually get
hair growing out of it.

479
00:29:36,300 --> 00:29:40,020
And the small and medium
ones don't really have an

480
00:29:40,020 --> 00:29:43,320
increased risk of
developing melanoma, it's

481
00:29:43,320 --> 00:29:46,200
equal to the general
population. However, the larger

482
00:29:46,200 --> 00:29:48,700
ones, the giant nevi,
the ones greater than 20

483
00:29:48,700 --> 00:29:52,260
centimeters, they do
have a risk of developing

484
00:29:52,400 --> 00:29:55,260
melanoma. But the removal is

485
00:29:55,260 --> 00:29:57,160
very, very, very difficult.

486
00:29:57,660 --> 00:30:00,060
40% of melanomas in kids do

487
00:30:00,060 --> 00:30:02,480
develop within these nevi.

488
00:30:05,000 --> 00:30:07,120
Okay, here's the
next case. What do

489
00:30:07,120 --> 00:30:09,220
you do next? Here
you have a patient.

490
00:30:10,020 --> 00:30:13,000
She has a little lesion here.

491
00:30:13,140 --> 00:30:16,980
What happens 11 months
later? Look at this lesion,

492
00:30:16,980 --> 00:30:19,360
how big it got, right?
So what do you do next?

493
00:30:21,180 --> 00:30:25,140
You look at the
ABCDEs of melanoma.

494
00:30:25,140 --> 00:30:28,500
That's what you do.
You want to see if that

495
00:30:28,500 --> 00:30:32,460
lesion has any of the
ABCDEs of melanoma.

496
00:30:32,500 --> 00:30:35,410
So the first thing you
look at is asymmetry.

497
00:30:36,300 --> 00:30:39,520
You cut this in half.
is it symmetrical or

498
00:30:39,520 --> 00:30:43,400
asymmetrical it's asymmetrical
you have this on this

499
00:30:43,400 --> 00:30:46,340
side and this on this side
it does not look the same

500
00:30:46,340 --> 00:30:50,840
correct the next is border
irregularity look at

501
00:30:50,840 --> 00:30:55,570
this border how irregular
this border is right so

502
00:30:55,570 --> 00:30:59,220
that's a sign of melanoma
look at the color

503
00:30:59,220 --> 00:31:03,580
variation look at this is
black this is light brown.

504
00:31:03,700 --> 00:31:06,840
So the color is, there's

505
00:31:06,840 --> 00:31:08,880
differences in
the color, right?

506
00:31:09,080 --> 00:31:11,800
Here you have diameter
greater than six

507
00:31:11,800 --> 00:31:14,320
millimeters. If you measure
this, it's greater than

508
00:31:14,320 --> 00:31:17,460
six millimeters. That's
a sign of melanoma.

509
00:31:18,500 --> 00:31:22,800
And the last one is
evolving. You see here, and

510
00:31:22,800 --> 00:31:26,940
you see evolving into
this. So this is a sign of

511
00:31:26,940 --> 00:31:29,740
melanoma. So what are the
risk factors of melanoma?

512
00:31:30,460 --> 00:31:33,420
Moles, especially
irregular ones,

513
00:31:33,420 --> 00:31:35,080
greater than five on a patient.

514
00:31:36,100 --> 00:31:38,560
Common moles greater
than 50 on a patient.

515
00:31:38,840 --> 00:31:40,300
Red hair and freckling.

516
00:31:40,900 --> 00:31:44,540
Inability to tan, right? So
if you're very light, fair

517
00:31:44,540 --> 00:31:48,040
-skinned, you have an increased
risk. Severe sunburn,

518
00:31:48,260 --> 00:31:50,500
any kind of sunburn,
but especially under

519
00:31:50,500 --> 00:31:52,560
the age of 14 with
a severe sunburn,

520
00:31:52,680 --> 00:31:56,260
and family history.
So this is your

521
00:31:56,260 --> 00:32:01,260
malignant melanoma
risk, a mnemonic.

522
00:32:03,980 --> 00:32:08,340
This case, this is a 63
-year-old female, shows you a

523
00:32:08,340 --> 00:32:11,560
dark area under her toenail.
Now she thinks she stubbed

524
00:32:11,560 --> 00:32:14,180
her nail a few months
prior while working in the

525
00:32:14,180 --> 00:32:17,330
garden, so she thinks that
this is just from trauma

526
00:32:17,330 --> 00:32:23,960
but look at the nail it
extends from here all the ways

527
00:32:23,960 --> 00:32:27,840
to here and there's some
pigment where the nail bed

528
00:32:27,840 --> 00:32:32,880
is right so what's the
sign where you have pigment

529
00:32:33,120 --> 00:32:36,960
beyond the nail bed this is
called the Hutchinson sign

530
00:32:37,280 --> 00:32:40,980
and these are longitudinal
pigmented streaks that

531
00:32:40,980 --> 00:32:45,440
extend from the proximal
or lateral nail fold out.

532
00:32:45,980 --> 00:32:48,960
So this could be a
sign of melanoma.

533
00:32:49,800 --> 00:32:52,220
Acral antigenous melanoma,

534
00:32:52,220 --> 00:32:56,020
70% of these melanomas
occur in African-American

535
00:32:56,020 --> 00:32:59,480
patients, and they're
located on the acral areas

536
00:32:59,480 --> 00:33:02,880
of the body, such as the
palms, the soles, the

537
00:33:02,880 --> 00:33:05,100
nail beds, the mucous
membranes, and they have

538
00:33:05,100 --> 00:33:09,200
a very poor prognosis.
They tend to metastasize

539
00:33:09,200 --> 00:33:12,110
early. So you really want
to make this diagnosis

540
00:33:15,420 --> 00:33:18,240
And that concludes
this lecture.